{"id":"ABA-383","title":"N08 — Reference sweep + fresh-install check","description":"## What

Re-point or remove every cross-cutting reference to a deleted or folded skill:

* README tables;
* `rules/PRODUCT_RULES.md`;
* the three `references/*.md` files;
* the idea-bank triage baseline;
* instruction files (`AGENTS.md:19` cites `initiative-shape`);
* `hooks/` (named by KR3);
* the `plugin.json` description (JSON, invisible to KR3's `*.md` grep — swept explicitly);
* `bin/eval-triggers` and the `eval/` fixtures (hardcoded skill names);
* the `install.sh` help text (`:161–173`);
* `docs/delivery-shape-contract.md` path citations;
* remaining cross-skill citations, including initiative C's plan delegating to `product-spike`.

The sweep note defines the allowlist: predecessor frontmatter, CHANGELOG history, and historical records under `docs/` are intentional; everything else is dangling.

## Why

A deleted skill that stays referenced is worse than one that never existed — the next agent follows the citation into a 404 and improvises. This closes D3 and leaves the pack coherent for initiative C's pointer-only workers.

Rejected: incremental sweeps inside each phase-skill node — four partial sweeps with no single proof point.

## Completion

* Done when: the KR3 grep (deleted names plus idea-triage / backend-spike / product-spike) over tracked markdown and the non-markdown live surfaces (`bin/`, `eval/`, `install.sh`, plugin.json) returns only allowlisted mentions.
* Done when: `install.sh` on a clean target yields exactly the four phase-skill wrappers plus utility wrappers and `shape-*` symlinks, and `uninstall.sh` removes them all.

## Assumptions

* CHANGELOG and docs-history mentions count as "intentional" under the KR *(to-verify — the sweep note proposes the allowlist explicitly and the owner confirms it)*
* Phase-skill nodes deleted their own directories and wrappers *(verified — N03/N04/N05 each carry a deletion task; this node's grep catches any miss)*

## Key Risks

* Out-of-repo consumers (drain-cycle prompts, user-level CLAUDE.md, initiative C's plan files) still cite folded names. Mitigation: C's `delegates_to` lines are grepped explicitly; anything outside this repo is recorded in the sweep note as a follow-up, not silently skipped.

